#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.autoRefreshIndex`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:10
msgid ""
"When using `git diff` to compare with work tree files, do not consider "
"stat-only changes as changed.  Instead, silently run `git update-index "
"--refresh` to update the cached stat information for paths whose contents in "
"the work tree match the contents in the index.  This option defaults to "
"`true`.  Note that this affects only `git diff` Porcelain, and not lower "
"level `diff` commands such as `git diff-files`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.dirstat`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tA comma separated list of `--dirstat` parameters specifying the\n"
"\tdefault behavior of the `--dirstat` option to `git diff` and friends.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tA comma separated list of `--dirstat` parameters specifying the\n"
"\tdefault behavior of the `--dirstat` option to linkgit:git-diff[1]\n"
"\tand friends.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tThe defaults can be overridden on the command line\n"
"\t(using `--dirstat=<param>,...`). The fallback defaults\n"
"\t(when not changed by `diff.dirstat`) are `changes,noncumulative,3`.\n"
"\tThe following parameters are available:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "`changes`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:33
msgid ""
"Compute the dirstat numbers by counting the lines that have been removed "
"from the source, or added to the destination. This ignores the amount of "
"pure code movements within a file.  In other words, rearranging lines in a "
"file is not counted as much as other changes.  This is the default behavior "
"when no parameter is given."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "`lines`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:41
msgid ""
"Compute the dirstat numbers by doing the regular line-based diff analysis, "
"and summing the removed/added line counts. (For binary files, count 64-byte "
"chunks instead, since binary files have no natural concept of lines). This "
"is a more expensive `--dirstat` behavior than the `changes` behavior, but it "
"does count rearranged lines within a file as much as other changes. The "
"resulting output is consistent with what you get from the other `--*stat` "
"options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "`files`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:46
msgid ""
"Compute the dirstat numbers by counting the number of files changed.  Each "
"changed file counts equally in the dirstat analysis. This is the "
"computationally cheapest `--dirstat` behavior, since it does not have to "
"look at the file contents at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "`cumulative`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:51
msgid ""
"Count changes in a child directory for the parent directory as well.  Note "
"that when using `cumulative`, the sum of the percentages reported may exceed "
"100%. The default (non-cumulative) behavior can be specified with the "
"`noncumulative` parameter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<limit>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:55
msgid ""
"An integer parameter specifies a cut-off percent (3% by default).  "
"Directories contributing less than this percentage of the changes are not "
"shown in the output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:61
msgid ""
"Example: The following will count changed files, while ignoring directories "
"with less than 10% of the total amount of changed files, and accumulating "
"child directory counts in the parent directories: `files,10,cumulative`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.statNameWidth`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:65
msgid ""
"Limit the width of the filename part in `--stat` output. If set, applies to "
"all commands generating `--stat` output except `format-patch`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.statGraphWidth`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:69
msgid ""
"Limit the width of the graph part in `--stat` output. If set, applies to all "
"commands generating `--stat` output except `format-patch`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.context`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:73
msgid ""
"Generate diffs with _<n>_ lines of context instead of the default of 3. This "
"value is overridden by the `-U` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.interHunkContext`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:79
msgid ""
"Show the context between diff hunks, up to the specified number of lines, "
"thereby fusing the hunks that are close to each other.  This value serves as "
"the default for the `--inter-hunk-context` command line option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.external`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:88
msgid ""
"If this config variable is set, diff generation is not performed using the "
"internal diff machinery, but using the given command.  Can be overridden "
"with the `GIT_EXTERNAL_DIFF` environment variable.  The command is called "
"with parameters as described under \"git Diffs\" in linkgit:git[1].  Note: "
"if you want to use an external diff program only on a subset of your files, "
"you might want to use linkgit:gitattributes[5] instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.trustExitCode`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:97
msgid ""
"If this boolean value is set to `true` then the `diff.external` command is "
"expected to return exit code 0 if it considers the input files to be equal "
"or 1 if it considers them to be different, like `diff`(1).  If it is set to "
"`false`, which is the default, then the command is expected to return exit "
"code `0` regardless of equality.  Any other exit code causes Git to report a "
"fatal error."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.ignoreSubmodules`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:110
msgid ""
"Sets the default value of `--ignore-submodules`. Note that this affects only "
"`git diff` Porcelain, and not lower level `diff` commands such as `git "
"diff-files`. `git checkout` and `git switch` also honor this setting when "
"reporting uncommitted changes. Setting it to `all` disables the submodule "
"summary normally shown by `git commit` and `git status` when "
"`status.submoduleSummary` is set unless it is overridden by using the "
"`--ignore-submodules` command-line option.  The `git submodule` commands are "
"not affected by this setting.  By default this is set to untracked so that "
"any untracked submodules are ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.mnemonicPrefix`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:116
msgid ""
"If set, `git diff` uses a prefix pair that is different from the standard "
"`a/` and `b/` depending on what is being compared.  When this configuration "
"is in effect, reverse diff output also swaps the order of the prefixes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "`git diff`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:118
msgid "compares the (i)ndex and the (w)ork tree;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "`git diff HEAD`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:120
msgid "compares a (c)ommit and the (w)ork tree;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "`git diff --cached`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:122
msgid "compares a (c)ommit and the (i)ndex;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "`git diff HEAD:<file1> <file2>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:124
msgid "compares an (o)bject and a (w)ork tree entity;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "`git diff --no-index <a> <b>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:126
msgid "compares two non-git things _<a>_ and _<b>_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.noPrefix`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:129
msgid "If set, `git diff` does not show any source or destination prefix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.srcPrefix`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:132
msgid "If set, `git diff` uses this source prefix. Defaults to `a/`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:133
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.dstPrefix`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:135
msgid "If set, `git diff` uses this destination prefix. Defaults to `b/`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.relative`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:139
msgid ""
"If set to `true`, `git diff` does not show changes outside of the directory "
"and show pathnames relative to the current directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:140
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.orderFile`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:142
msgid "File indicating how to order files within a diff."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:144
#, no-wrap
msgid "\tSee the `-O` option for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "\tSee the `-O` option to linkgit:git-diff[1] for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tIf `diff.orderFile` is a relative pathname, it is treated as\n"
"\trelative to the top of the working tree.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.renameLimit`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:156
msgid ""
"The number of files to consider in the exhaustive portion of copy/rename "
"detection; equivalent to the `git diff` option `-l`.  If not set, the "
"default value is currently 1000.  This setting has no effect if rename "
"detection is turned off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.renames`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:165
msgid ""
"Whether and how Git detects renames.  If set to `false`, rename detection is "
"disabled. If set to `true`, basic rename detection is enabled.  If set to "
"`copies` or `copy`, Git will detect copies, as well.  Defaults to `true`.  "
"Note that this affects only `git diff` Porcelain like linkgit:git-diff[1] "
"and linkgit:git-log[1], and not lower level commands such as "
"linkgit:git-diff-files[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:166
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.suppressBlankEmpty`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:169
msgid ""
"A boolean to inhibit the standard behavior of printing a space before each "
"empty output line. Defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.submodule`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:177
msgid ""
"Specify the format in which differences in submodules are shown.  The "
"`short` format just shows the names of the commits at the beginning and end "
"of the range. The `log` format lists the commits in the range like "
"linkgit:git-submodule[1] `summary` does. The `diff` format shows an inline "
"diff of the changed contents of the submodule. Defaults to `short`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.wordRegex`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:183
msgid ""
"A POSIX Extended Regular Expression used to determine what is a \"word\" "
"when performing word-by-word difference calculations.  Character sequences "
"that match the regular expression are \"words\", all other characters are "
"*ignorable* whitespace."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:184
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.<driver>.command`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:187
msgid "The custom diff driver command.  See linkgit:gitattributes[5] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:188
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.<driver>.trustExitCode`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:196
msgid ""
"If this boolean value is set to `true` then the `diff.<driver>.command` "
"command is expected to return exit code 0 if it considers the input files to "
"be equal or 1 if it considers them to be different, like `diff`(1).  If it "
"is set to `false`, which is the default, then the command is expected to "
"return exit code 0 regardless of equality.  Any other exit code causes Git "
"to report a fatal error."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.<driver>.xfuncname`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:201
msgid ""
"The regular expression that the diff driver should use to recognize the hunk "
"header.  A built-in pattern may also be used.  See linkgit:gitattributes[5] "
"for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.<driver>.binary`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:205
msgid ""
"Set this option to `true` to make the diff driver treat files as binary.  "
"See linkgit:gitattributes[5] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:206
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.<driver>.textconv`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:211
msgid ""
"The command that the diff driver should call to generate the text-converted "
"version of a file.  The result of the conversion is used to generate a "
"human-readable diff.  See linkgit:gitattributes[5] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:212
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.<driver>.wordRegex`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:216
msgid ""
"The regular expression that the diff driver should use to split words in a "
"line.  See linkgit:gitattributes[5] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:217
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.<driver>.cachetextconv`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:220
msgid ""
"Set this option to `true` to make the diff driver cache the text conversion "
"outputs.  See linkgit:gitattributes[5] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:223
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.indentHeuristic`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:226
msgid ""
"Set this option to `false` to disable the default heuristics that shift diff "
"hunk boundaries to make patches easier to read."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:227
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.algorithm`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:229
msgid "Choose a diff algorithm.  The variants are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:231
#, no-wrap
msgid "`default`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:232
#, no-wrap
msgid "`myers`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:234
msgid "The basic greedy diff algorithm. Currently, this is the default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:234
#, no-wrap
msgid "`minimal`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:237
msgid "Spend extra time to make sure the smallest possible diff is produced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "`patience`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:239
msgid "Use \"patience diff\" algorithm when generating patches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:239
#, no-wrap
msgid "`histogram`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:242
msgid ""
"This algorithm extends the patience algorithm to \"support low-occurrence "
"common elements\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:245
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.wsErrorHighlight`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:253
msgid ""
"Highlight whitespace errors in the `context`, `old` or `new` lines of the "
"diff.  Multiple values are separated by comma, `none` resets previous "
"values, `default` reset the list to `new` and `all` is a shorthand for "
"`old,new,context`.  The whitespace errors are colored with "
"`color.diff.whitespace`.  The command line option "
"`--ws-error-highlight=<kind>` overrides this setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:254
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.colorMoved`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:257
msgid ""
"If set to either a valid _<mode>_ or a `true` value, moved lines in a diff "
"are colored differently."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:259
#, no-wrap
msgid "\tFor details of valid modes see `--color-moved`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:262
#, no-wrap
msgid "\tFor details of valid modes see `--color-moved` in linkgit:git-diff[1].\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:265
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tIf simply set to `true` the default color mode will be used. When\n"
"\tset to `false`, moved lines are not colored.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:266
#, no-wrap
msgid "`diff.colorMovedWS`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/diff.txt:269
msgid ""
"When moved lines are colored using e.g. the `diff.colorMoved` setting, this "
"option controls the mode how spaces are treated.  For details of valid modes "
"see `--color-moved-ws` in linkgit:git-diff[1]."
msgstr ""
